      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-bottom:6pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">SCPSC Docket No. 2024-34-E</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-bottom:6pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Pursuant to the Comprehensive Settlement Agreement approved by the SCPSC in DESC's Retail Electric Base Rate Case (Docket No. 2024-34-E), the SCPSC approved a Storm Rider effective September 1, 2024, which includes annual customer collections of $1,500,000 for recovery of qualified storm cost deferrals. In late September 2024, DESC incurred significant incremental restoration storm costs related to Hurricane Helene. These incremental cost deferrals exceeded the current customer collections which resulted in a regulatory asset.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-49" id="fn-49" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
